Backport of lxc/incus@75543793daa396d61e2f8d16e1e8a62c62a79c9e (stable-7.0; on main as
5b6354a24) to v7.0.2 for the isx appliance (Sanne/incus-spawn#2739), unchanged: part of the fix
for GHSA-fg2p-r659-c4q8. An instance on the bridge could remove or take over another instance's
DNS name with forged DHCP messages, despite security.mac_filtering. dnsmasq now ignores the
names DHCP clients send in managed mode, and the NIC's bridge filter drops DHCP requests whose
client hardware address is not the NIC's. Remove this file once INCUS_VERSION is a release that
contains the commit (the next 7.0 release; 7.0.3 is not out yet).

From 75543793daa396d61e2f8d16e1e8a62c62a79c9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?St=C3=A9phane=20Graber?= <stgraber@stgraber.org>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:03:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] incusd/network: Keep instances from claiming other instances'
 DNS names
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

dnsmasq accepted a DHCPRELEASE naming another instance's lease and then
gave that instance's name to any client requesting it. Managed mode
now ignores client-supplied names, and MAC-filtered NICs may only send
DHCPv4 requests for their own hardware address.

This addresses GHSA-fg2p-r659-c4q8 (CVE pending)

Signed-off-by: Stéphane Graber <stgraber@stgraber.org>
(cherry picked from commit 75543793daa396d61e2f8d16e1e8a62c62a79c9e)
---
 .../server/firewall/drivers/drivers_nftables_templates.go    | 4 ++++
 internal/server/network/driver_bridge.go                     | 5 +++++
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/internal/server/firewall/drivers/drivers_nftables_templates.go b/internal/server/firewall/drivers/drivers_nftables_templates.go
index 19d3ea9fb..7b5423d50 100644
--- a/internal/server/firewall/drivers/drivers_nftables_templates.go
+++ b/internal/server/firewall/drivers/drivers_nftables_templates.go
@@ -227,6 +227,8 @@ chain in{{.chainSeparator}}{{.deviceLabel}} {
 	iifname "{{.hostName}}" ether saddr != {{.hwAddr}} drop
 	iifname "{{.hostName}}" ether type arp arp saddr ether != {{.hwAddr}} drop
 	iifname "{{.hostName}}" ether type ip6 icmpv6 type 136 @nh,528,48 != {{.hwAddrHex}} drop
+	iifname "{{.hostName}}" ether type ip ip frag-off & 0x2000 != 0 udp dport 67 drop
+	iifname "{{.hostName}}" ether type ip udp dport 67 @th,288,48 != {{.hwAddrHex}} drop
 	{{ end }}
 
 	{{ if .filterUnwantedFrames }}
@@ -306,6 +308,8 @@ chain fwd{{.chainSeparator}}{{.deviceLabel}} {
 	iifname "{{.hostName}}" ether saddr != {{.hwAddr}} drop
 	iifname "{{.hostName}}" ether type arp arp saddr ether != {{.hwAddr}} drop
 	iifname "{{.hostName}}" ether type ip6 icmpv6 type 136 @nh,528,48 != {{.hwAddrHex}} drop
+	iifname "{{.hostName}}" ether type ip ip frag-off & 0x2000 != 0 udp dport 67 drop
+	iifname "{{.hostName}}" ether type ip udp dport 67 @th,288,48 != {{.hwAddrHex}} drop
 	{{ end }}
 
 	{{ if .filterUnwantedFrames }}
diff --git a/internal/server/network/driver_bridge.go b/internal/server/network/driver_bridge.go
index 1341df107..271092b4c 100644
--- a/internal/server/network/driver_bridge.go
+++ b/internal/server/network/driver_bridge.go
@@ -1959,6 +1959,11 @@ func (n *bridge) setup(oldConfig map[string]string) error {
 			dnsmasqCmd = append(dnsmasqCmd, "-S", fmt.Sprintf("/%s/", dnsDomain))
 		}
 
+		// Only use the generated names in managed mode, ignoring those supplied by DHCP clients.
+		if n.config["dns.mode"] == "" || n.config["dns.mode"] == "managed" {
+			dnsmasqCmd = append(dnsmasqCmd, "--dhcp-ignore-names")
+		}
+
 		// Don't serve the host's /etc/hosts entries.
 		if util.IsFalse(n.config["dns.include_hosts"]) {
 			dnsmasqCmd = append(dnsmasqCmd, "--no-hosts")
